window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2d22af6e58ee6112"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"adopt-liquid-glass\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"liquid-glass\">采用 Liquid Glass</h1> <p>使用 Codex 和 iOS 26 API、Xcode 26，将现有 SwiftUI 应用迁移到 Liquid Glass。</p> <p>使用 Codex 和 Build iOS Apps 插件审查现有 iPhone 与 iPad 界面，用原生 Liquid Glass 替换自定义模糊或材质堆叠，并通过 iOS 26 可用性检查和模拟器验证，确保迁移安全。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要切实可行的 iOS 26 Liquid Glass 迁移方案、而不是笼统改版说明的现有 SwiftUI 应用。</li> <li>希望 Codex 审查自定义卡片、表单、标签栏、工具栏和操作按钮，再分步骤完成迁移的团队。</li> <li>仍支持较旧 iOS 版本、需要通过 <code>#available(iOS 26, *)</code> 回退兼容，而不是一次性改成单一视觉方案的应用。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 SwiftUI Liquid Glass、SwiftUI 界面模式和模拟器调试技能，更新 iOS 界面、采用原生玻璃效果，并在 iOS 26 模拟器上验证结果。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Liquid Glass 界面 API</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI（需联网）</a> 搭配 <code>glassEffect</code>、<code>GlassEffectContainer</code> 和玻璃按钮样式</td> <td>这些是技能应优先采用的原生 API，可让 Codex 移除自定义模糊层，而不是重新实现材质系统。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>平台基线</td> <td>iOS 26 和 Xcode 26</td> <td>Liquid Glass 随 iOS 26 SDK 提供。Codex 应使用 Xcode 26 构建，并为更早的系统版本加入明确的回退方案。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>模拟器验证</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP（需联网）</a></td> <td>进行视觉迁移时，需要构建、启动、截图和检查日志，尤其是在审阅多个状态和设备尺寸时。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>将一个流程迁移到 Liquid Glass</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Build iOS Apps 插件及其 SwiftUI Liquid Glass 技能，将此应用中一个流量较高的流程迁移到 Liquid Glass。\n\n约束：\n- 将其视为 iOS 26 + Xcode 26 迁移，但对于较早的部署目标，必须通过 `#available(iOS 26, *)` 保留非玻璃效果的回退方案。\n- 先审查该流程。指出应改用原生 Liquid Glass 的自定义背景、模糊堆叠、标签、按钮、表单和工具栏；也指出哪些界面应继续保持普通内容样式。\n- 优先使用系统控件和原生 API，例如 `glassEffect`、`GlassEffectContainer`、`glassEffectID`、`.buttonStyle(.glass)` 和 `.buttonStyle(.glassProminent)`，而不是自定义模糊效果。只有当形变过渡确实能改善流程时，才将 `glassEffectID` 与 `@Namespace` 配合使用。\n- 在布局和视觉修饰符之后应用 `glassEffect`，让材质包裹最终需要的形状；形状保持一致；只在确实响应触控的控件上使用 `.interactive()`。\n- 使用 XcodeBuildMCP 在 iOS 26 模拟器上构建并运行，为迁移后的流程截取屏幕截图，并准确说明使用的 scheme、模拟器和检查项。\n\n交付：\n- 该流程的精简迁移计划\n- 已实现的 Liquid Glass 功能片段\n- iOS 26 之前设备上的回退行为\n- 你执行的模拟器验证步骤和所用截图\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-from-the-ios-26-baseline\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ios-26\">从 iOS 26 基线开始</h2> <p>首先把 Liquid Glass 当作 iOS 26 和 Xcode 26 迁移项目。使用 iOS 26 SDK 重新构建应用，先检查标准 SwiftUI 控件自动呈现的效果；之后再让 Codex 改造那些仍显得过于扁平、厚重，或与系统界面脱节的自定义部分。</p> <p>如果应用仍须支持早期 iOS 版本，请一开始就明确这个约束。来自 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>的 SwiftUI Liquid Glass 技能，应使用 <code>#available(iOS 26, *)</code> 控制仅支持玻璃效果的新 API，并保留一条在较旧设备上也清晰易读的回退路径。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-the-ios-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ios\">使用 iOS 插件</h2> <p>如果希望 Codex 结合 SwiftUI 界面改动与基于模拟器的验证，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>。处理 Liquid Glass 时，建议让 Codex 先审查一个流程，迁移少量界面，在 iOS 26 模拟器上启动应用，并在扩大范围前截取屏幕截图。</p> <p>该插件包含 SwiftUI Liquid Glass 技能，其中有几条适合写进提示词的简单默认规则：</p> <ul> <li>优先采用原生 <code>glassEffect</code>、<code>GlassEffectContainer</code>、玻璃按钮样式和 <code>glassEffectID</code> 过渡，不要先用自定义模糊视图。</li> <li>在布局与视觉修饰符之后应用 <code>.glassEffect(...)</code>，确保材质作用于最终形状。</li> <li>多个玻璃界面同时出现时，用 <code>GlassEffectContainer</code> 包裹彼此相关的元素。</li> <li>只在按钮、标签和确实会响应触控的控件上使用 <code>.interactive()</code>。</li> <li>在整个功能中保持圆角、着色和间距一致，不要混用彼此无关的玻璃效果。</li> <li>为 iOS 26 之前的目标系统保留非玻璃效果的回退方案。</li> </ul> <p>如需了解如何安装插件和技能，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（本地尚未收录）</a>和<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能（本地尚未收录）</a>文档。</p> <p><a id=\"watch-the-wwdc-sessions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"wwdc\">查看 WWDC 讲座</h2> <p>在要求 Codex 改造真实生产流程前，以下 WWDC25 讲座值得参考：</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/219/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">认识 Liquid Glass（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/356/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">了解新的设计系统（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/323/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用新设计构建 SwiftUI 应用（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/284/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用新设计构建 UIKit 应用（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/256/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI 新功能（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"prompt-a-migration-plan-then-a-slice\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">先让它规划迁移，再实现一小部分</h2> <p>把“哪些地方应该使用玻璃效果？”和“现在就把所有代码写出来”分开，Liquid Glass 迁移会更顺利。先让 Codex 快速审查，再让它实现一个独立的功能片段，并通过模拟器验证。</p> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">实用建议</h2> <p><a id=\"do-not-glass-everything\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">不要给所有界面都套上玻璃效果</h3> <p>Liquid Glass 应营造位于内容之上的清晰控件层，而不是把每张卡片都变成发光面板。请 Codex 移除与系统材质冲突的装饰背景；在可读性更重要的地方保留普通内容；只在需要语义强调或突出主要操作时使用着色。</p> <p><a id=\"start-with-one-high-traffic-flow\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">从一个高频流程开始</h3> <p>标签页根视图、详情屏幕、表单、搜索界面或引导流程，通常都比全应用范围的改造更适合作为起点。这样更便于审阅，也能更清楚地判断哪些 Liquid Glass 设计应该沉淀为可复用的组件模式。</p> <p><a id=\"review-fallback-behavior-deliberately\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">有意审阅回退行为</h3> <p>如果部署目标低于 iOS 26，请让 Codex 同时展示 Liquid Glass 版本和回退实现。这样能及早发现 API 可用性回归，避免发布一个只能在最新版模拟器中运行的迁移。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"adopt-liquid-glass\">Adopt liquid glass</h1> <p>Use Codex to migrate an existing SwiftUI app to Liquid Glass with iOS 26 APIs and Xcode 26.</p> <p>Use Codex and the Build iOS Apps plugin to audit existing iPhone and iPad UI, replace custom blur or material stacks with native Liquid Glass, and keep the migration safe with iOS 26 availability checks and simulator-driven validation.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Existing SwiftUI apps that need a practical iOS 26 Liquid Glass migration plan, not a vague redesign brief</li> <li>Teams that want Codex to audit custom cards, sheets, tab bars, toolbars, and action buttons and then implement the migration slice by slice</li> <li>Apps that still support older iOS versions and need <code>#available(iOS 26, *)</code> fallbacks instead of a one-way visual rewrite</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-ios-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the SwiftUI Liquid Glass, SwiftUI UI patterns, and simulator debugging skills to modernize iOS screens, adopt native glass effects, and verify the result on iOS 26 simulators.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Liquid Glass UI APIs</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI (online)</a> with <code>glassEffect</code>, <code>GlassEffectContainer</code>, and glass button styles</td> <td>These are the native APIs the skill should reach for first, so Codex removes custom blur layers instead of reinventing the material system.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Platform baseline</td> <td>iOS 26 and Xcode 26</td> <td>Liquid Glass lands with the iOS 26 SDK. Codex should compile with Xcode 26 and add explicit fallbacks for earlier OS support.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Simulator validation</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.xcodebuildmcp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XcodeBuildMCP (online)</a></td> <td>Build, launch, screenshot, and log inspection matter during a visual migration, especially when reviewing multiple states and device sizes.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Migrate One Flow to Liquid Glass</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build iOS Apps plugin and its SwiftUI Liquid Glass skill to migrate one high-traffic flow in this app to Liquid Glass.\n\nConstraints:\n- Treat this as an iOS 26 + Xcode 26 migration, but preserve a non-glass fallback for earlier deployment targets with `#available(iOS 26, *)`.\n- Audit the flow first. Call out custom backgrounds, blur stacks, chips, buttons, sheets, and toolbars that should become native Liquid Glass and call out surfaces that should stay plain content.\n- Prefer system controls and native APIs like `glassEffect`, `GlassEffectContainer`, `glassEffectID`, `.buttonStyle(.glass)`, and `.buttonStyle(.glassProminent)` over custom blurs. Use `glassEffectID` with `@Namespace` only when a real morphing transition improves the flow.\n- Apply `glassEffect` after layout and visual modifiers, keep shapes consistent, and use `.interactive()` only on controls that actually respond to touch.\n- Use XcodeBuildMCP to build and run on an iOS 26 simulator, capture screenshots for the migrated flow, and mention exactly which scheme, simulator, and checks you used.\n\nDeliver:\n- a concise migration plan for the flow\n- the implemented Liquid Glass slice\n- the fallback behavior for pre-iOS 26 devices\n- the simulator validation steps and screenshots you used\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-from-the-ios-26-baseline\">Start from the iOS 26 baseline</h2> <p>Treat Liquid Glass as an iOS 26 and Xcode 26 migration project first. Rebuild the app with the iOS 26 SDK, inspect what you get automatically from standard SwiftUI controls, and only then ask Codex to redesign the custom parts that still look too flat, too heavy, or too detached from system chrome.</p> <p>If the app still supports earlier iOS versions, make that constraint explicit up front. The SwiftUI Liquid Glass skill in the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a> should gate new glass-only APIs with <code>#available(iOS 26, *)</code> and keep a fallback path that still reads well on older devices.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-the-ios-plugin\">Leverage the iOS plugin</h2> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-ios-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build iOS Apps plugin (online)</a> when you want Codex to combine SwiftUI UI changes with simulator-backed verification. For Liquid Glass work, the useful move is to ask Codex to audit one flow, migrate a small set of surfaces, launch the result on an iOS 26 simulator, and capture screenshots before expanding the scope.</p> <p>That plugin includes a SwiftUI Liquid Glass skill with a simple set of defaults worth carrying into your prompt:</p> <ul> <li>Prefer native <code>glassEffect</code>, <code>GlassEffectContainer</code>, glass button styles, and <code>glassEffectID</code> transitions over custom blur views.</li> <li>Apply <code>.glassEffect(...)</code> after layout and visual modifiers so the material wraps the final shape you actually want.</li> <li>Wrap related glass elements in <code>GlassEffectContainer</code> when multiple surfaces appear together.</li> <li>Use <code>.interactive()</code> only on buttons, chips, and controls that actually respond to touch.</li> <li>Keep corner shapes, tinting, and spacing consistent across the feature instead of mixing one-off glass treatments.</li> <li>Preserve a non-glass fallback for pre-iOS 26 targets.</li> </ul> <p>To learn more about installing plugins and skills, see our <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins (not in this local snapshot)</a> and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skills (not in this local snapshot)</a> docs.</p> <h2 id=\"watch-the-wwdc-sessions\">Watch the WWDC sessions</h2> <p>These WWDC25 sessions are a good reference set before you ask Codex to refactor a real production flow:</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/219/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Meet Liquid Glass (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/356/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Get to know the new design system (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/323/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a SwiftUI app with the new design (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/284/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a UIKit app with the new design (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2025/256/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">What's new in SwiftUI (online)</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"prompt-a-migration-plan-then-a-slice\">Prompt a migration plan, then a slice</h2> <p>Liquid Glass migrations go better when Codex separates \"where should glass appear?\" from \"write all the code now.\" Ask for a quick audit first, then let the agent implement one self-contained slice with simulator verification.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"do-not-glass-everything\">Do not glass everything</h3> <p>Liquid Glass should create a clear control layer above content, not turn every card into a glowing panel. Ask Codex to remove decorative backgrounds that fight system materials, preserve plain content where readability matters most, and reserve tinting for semantic emphasis or primary actions.</p> <h3 id=\"start-with-one-high-traffic-flow\">Start with one high-traffic flow</h3> <p>A tab root, detail screen, sheet, search surface, or onboarding flow is usually a better first migration target than a full app-wide sweep. That keeps review easier and makes it clear which Liquid Glass decisions should become reusable component patterns.</p> <h3 id=\"review-fallback-behavior-deliberately\">Review fallback behavior deliberately</h3> <p>If your deployment target is below iOS 26, ask Codex to show the fallback implementation alongside the Liquid Glass version. That review step catches accidental API availability regressions and avoids shipping a migration that only works on the latest simulator.</p>"};
